            <link>https://www.pbs.org/newshour/show/how-bags-of-ice-are-helping-save-lives-in-phoenix</link>
            <description><![CDATA[Extreme heat is the deadliest weather-related threat in the U.S. In Phoenix, heat kills more people than homicides each year. So the city is turning to an unlikely lifesaver: bags of ice. And the fire department is creating a new model in the battle against heatstroke. For our series, Tipping Point, Ben Tracy of Climate Central shows how this low-tech approach is saving lives.]]></description>
